  "markdown_content": "Professional athletes around the world are raising their voices about the impact of climate change on sports and athletic performance. In Baku, Azerbaijan, the effects are becoming increasingly apparent.\\n\\n## Athlete Impact\\n\\nPragnya Mohan, a veteran triathlete with nearly ten years of professional experience, has found herself unable to continue training in her native India due to extreme heat conditions. The rising temperatures have forced her to relocate her training base to the United Kingdom.\\n\\nThis relocation represents a growing trend among athletes who must adapt their training regimens and competition schedules to cope with changing climate conditions. Athletes are not just concerned about their performance but also about their health and safety as temperatures continue to rise globally.",
